// NEGATIVE TEST -- a top-level initialiser may not overflow i64 (N3-09).
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT A PEDANTIC RULE. Signed overflow is UNDEFINED in C, so the
// number this used to produce was not a wrong answer, it was an arbitrary one.
// Measured before the evaluator existed: this program compiled, linked, ran,
// exited 0 and printed -9223372036854775808, which is what one optimiser on one
// host chose to do with an expression the standard says nothing about.
//
// Every arithmetic operator is checked, so `*` and `-` and unary negation
// refuse the same way. What is still ACCEPTED is the value `i64` cannot spell
// directly: `-9223372036854775807 - 1` evaluates in range and is pinned by
// tests/03_const_items.pd.
const X: i64 = 9223372036854775807 + 1;

fn main() {
    print_int(X);
}
